WEBVTT

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.080
Please... take care of this child...

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.170
Is he alive?

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.480
I don't know.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.370
Is this... cold sleep?

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.690
Sure seems like it.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.550
He seems to be a boy.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:40.680
More importantly...

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.450
...is this guy even human?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.380
He does seem a little different.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.150
Was it this child who was calling out to Luna?

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.610
I don't know.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.100
This child...

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.290
Could it be he's an alien?

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.480
Don't be ridiculous!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.650
But look at that!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.110
I ain't got nothin' in my data like this script!

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.310
He may actually be an alien.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.490
Planetary settlement has progressed...

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.810
...but mankind has yet to encounter alien life.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:29.140
Then...

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.180
...this will be mankind's first contact with aliens!

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:34.980
In that case, we'll...

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.240
...be famous as the discoverers of aliens!

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.580
That's only if we ever get home from this planet, of course.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.380
But...

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.280
...that might not be impossible either!

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.160
The fact that this cold sleep chamber is working means...

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.410
...that the energy system is still active!

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.710
Let's look into it.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.220
We might be able to figure something out as well.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.190
Alrighty!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.270
Right, let's go!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.930
The controls...

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.220
...are too...

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.510
...high for me!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.440
Was it you...

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.040
...who called out to me?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:06.890
Wait a moment.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.900
Could it be...

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.350
...there's someone here besides that boy?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.240
You mean, hiding somewhere?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.980
But there doesn't seem to be any sign of other people.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.040
I don't see any doors, either.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:23.590
That's right!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.340
What are you trying to say?

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.590
Wha-- what is this?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.640
A planet?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.660
This isn't Earth, is it?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.460
It's a little similar, but different.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.330
It's a planet that ain't in my data.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.150
Then what planet is it?

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.930
This might be...

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.210
...the planet we're on now!

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.960
Then what are those marks?

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.600
I think they indicate the location of something.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.640
Was it you?

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.860
Was the one who called out to me...

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.470
...you?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.750
Luna, what's goin' on?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.010
He opened his eyes.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.230
He opened his eyes!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:10.860
It's true.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.430
Does this mean the cold sleep was deactivated?

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.540
Even if it were, it's too soon for him to be openin' his eyes.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.080
Then it was deactivated before we came in here?

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:30.040
Then you mean it predicted that we'd come here?

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.520
To think that something like that would be possible...

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.560
It wasn't this child, then?

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.150
Since he was cold sleeping, it would be impossible.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:38.390
Sure would.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.410
That voice that guided Luna here...

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:45.930
I can't think of anythin' but that that voice was managin' this place from somewhere else.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.240
.dlihc siht rof erac esaelP

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.330
This voice...

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.260
Where did it come from?

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:00.440
What's happenin'?

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.740
This is the voice we heard over Shingo's communications device!

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.660
Yes...

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:07.260
...that's right.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.770
.dlihc siht rof erac esaelP

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.020
Please... take care of this child...

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:20.730
"Please take care of this child"?

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:22.900
What does that mean?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:25.880
...erac esaelP

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:27.890
.dlihc siht rof...

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.340
What's it saying?

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:32.890
"Take care, take care."

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.660
Take care of this child?

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.030
You mean it wants us to raise this child?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.310
Alduram Gyet.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.330
Again!

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.430
What's he saying?

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.870
"Alduram Gyet."

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.130
What does it mean?

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.720
I don't know.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.380
Alduram Gyet.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.820
What just... happened?

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:44.710
He's clothed all of a sudden!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.980
It's not just clothes! Shoes too!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.030
Just now, it might 've been doin' somethin'.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.540
You don't mean... nano-machines?

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.240
Don't!

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.830
You shouldn't touch him yet.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:45.460
After wakin' up from a long cold sleep, his body's not at full strength.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.060
His skin might've become fragile.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.540
Keep it up!

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:13.880
Hey, Shingo!

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:15.930
Where are you going?

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.460
We forgot about the most important thing!

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.050
The communicator!

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:21.870
What about the communicator?

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.440
If these ruins have a communicator...

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.690
...we might be able to send out a powerful emergency beacon!

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:32.500
You mean help will come, and we'll be able to get off this planet?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.960
Alright! I'll look for it too!

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.380
You did it!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:44.780
Who are you?

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.060
Where are you from?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.040
Leave the questions until later.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.240
You're trying to stand up, right?

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:00.190
Go for it!

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:26.030
There's nothing that seems like a communicator.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:28.000
In that case, the random approach.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.920
Take that! Come on!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.130
What just happened?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:46.640
Over here, too.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.240
What happened?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:09.570
What's this?

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:10.510
A card?

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:12.720
The door!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:45.940
Let's hurry out of here!

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:47.580
You must be kidding!

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:50.070
There's still tons of things I want to look into!

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:51.460
You'll get shut in!

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:52.560
No!

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:53.990
No, no!

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:55.040
C'mon!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.970
--Stop being so unreasonable!
--Let go of me!

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.510
Let go of me!

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:00.270
Put me down!

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:04.750
Luna!

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:06.870
Luna, hurry!

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.370
It's okay, you go on ahead!

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.810
Hurry, hurry, Luna!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.960
Hurry it up!

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.090
I can't hold it anymore...

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.600
That was a close call.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.430
Are you okay?

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:38.780
Damn...

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:41.590
Why'd the door close?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.330
Howard, it's because you did something to cause it again!

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.810
What do you mean, 'again'?

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:49.130
It's the same as with the shuttle's release mechanism!

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:50.280
What?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.530
Have your fight later.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:52.410
Let's hurry.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:14.930
Come to think of it...

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.330
...the crab that was here when we came in...

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.410
It's disappeared?

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:21.850
Looks like it went somewhere.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.810
It may still be hiding somewhere.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.470
Open up!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.980
Luna, give it another try.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:40.960
No luck, huh?

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.900
But there was a mountain of riches inside!

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.030
Damn it!

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.850
Open up! Open up! Open up!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.180
Open... sesame!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.090
--You think it'll open if you do that?
--Sesame!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:57.100
Howard! Stop goofing off!

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.460
If I didn't try it, we couldn't be sure, right?

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:01.540
Maybe we can use this.

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:07.580
No luck after all.

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:09.180
Is this that...

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:10.230
Yep.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.490
The thing that came outta the cold sleep chamber.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.930
There may be another door.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.370
Let's split up and look for it.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.320
Alright... let's go!

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.730
Stay here, okay?

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:34.660
Luna, you stay with the kid.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.010
I understand. I won't go anywhere.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:03.870
Huh?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.200
Who might this be?

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.980
Um... this...

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:18.700
I was just cleaning up...

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.910
Never touch my things again.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.010
How did it go?

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:48.890
We went around the wall, sensin' all the way, but there didn't seem to be another entrance.

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:50.180
Really...

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:54.550
Chako, I wonder how long these ruins have been here.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:55.920
Let's see...

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:59.370
Based on the overgrowth of vines...

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.560
...I'd guess at least five hundred years've passed.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.370
F-- Five hundred years? You're lying.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:06.510
It's no lie!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:09.180
I wouldn't be surprised if it was a thousand.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:14.260
Then you're saying that this child may have been in cold sleep for a very long period?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.260
That might be true.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.780
Just who is this guy, anyways?

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.370
Where are you from?

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.180
Howard, don't speak so loudly!

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:28.510
That's right! It's no use askin' him!

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:31.470
He's an alien, so his language would be totally different.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:35.030
But why could Luna understand what was said?

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:36.700
I don't know.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.610
It's not that I could hear the words clearly...

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.180
...but somehow I felt like I knew the meaning.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:45.510
Telepathy?

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.560
That's the only explanation I can think of.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.540
Then that means...

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.690
...this little brat's got psychic powers too?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.290
Don't make me laugh!

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:00.760
If you make too much fun, he might make you disappear in an instant.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.360
If we don't hurry back to Everyone's House soon, the sun will set.

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:10.490
What should we do?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.980
Do we take the child back with us?

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.080
Of course that's what I planned to do.

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:22.080
Taking care of that child will put a strain on our lifestyle.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.710
Strain?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.500
Food, shelter, and various other things.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:29.260
I think we have to leave him to his own devices.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.530
We'll manage them all somehow.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:33.790
That's right, that's right!

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:36.400
It's too cruel just to leave him on his own!

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:40.940
This child is our precious clue to solving the riddle of this planet.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.110
I agree with Luna as well.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:45.960
I agree too!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.210
Luna was asked to take care of this kid by that voice, wasn't she?

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:50.930
Yes.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.880
In that case, we have to take good care of the kid...

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.650
...and when the owner of the voice comes for him...

00:19:56.890 --> 00:20:00.810
...we might be able to make off with a space ship while he's not looking!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.810
We should be grateful!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:05.970
I dunno if I should call it unscrupulous or shameful..

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:09.120
As long as everyone is agreed, I have no objections.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:11.670
Let's hurry home.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.770
What's Menori so angry about?

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:19.260
Anyways, let's go.

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:21.740
I'm sure Sharla and Kaoru are worried about us.

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:23.690
That's right.

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:26.290
Here.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.820
I've got an unsettlin' feelin'.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.180
Kaoru...

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:02.990
I'm sorry.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:03.980
Umm...

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:05.930
It really wasn't on purpose!

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:08.260
I found it by accident while I was cleaning.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.280
Is the boy in that picture...

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:15.080
...a friend?

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:18.660
I'm sorry.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:20.290
I'm asking weird questions.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.440
But I...

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.820
...feel a little relieved.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.680
Kaoru, even you have a friend like that.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.910
He's no longer with us.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:43.920
I killed him.

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:05.130
Look at Howard... he's so obliging.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:07.430
Offering to keep an eye on that boy!

00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:12.160
He's prob'ly just happy havin' someone who listens to what he says.

00:23:12.680 --> 00:23:14.930
He's taken a shine to the little squirt.

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:17.630
Just like a big brother.

00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:20.280
Maybe so, but he still has a dangerous moment.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.530
A formidable opponent appears!

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:27.790
Next time: A-da-m
